{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages","id":1395545,"title":"Can Arhats combat mages?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-10T01:19:04-07:00","id":1395545,"title":"Can Arhats combat mages?","content":"SO Arhats are incredibly powerful beings. What is the extent of their powers compared to mages?<br /> <br /> What kind of powers do Arhats have?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T01:22:59-07:00","id":1395546,"title":"","content":"You mean Dharma 10 Wan Gui ?<br /> <br /> They resemble 3rd gens Methseulah in Golconda, and almost the embodies of their own Dharma<br /> They have access to level 10 KotE Disciplines in theory (if these powers do exist, though). Wan gui disciplines much like kindred ones<br /> They may have great social bonus when facing lesser wan gui<br /> <br /> Unfortunately not much canon concerns advanced wan gui powers, especially 9-10 ones, so, know little in general. But I think they could have a fight with archmages or even 3rd gens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-10-2020, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:07:12-07:00","id":1395549,"title":"","content":"Well, given that Ravnos was fought by three Bodhisattvas (Minimum Dharma of 9) for a couple of days non-stop in the Week Of Nightmares, I think it's safe to say that Arhats (Minimum Dharma of 10) can do the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:14:06-07:00","id":1395550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395549#post1395549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, given that Ravnos was fought by three Bodhisattvas (Minimum Dharma of 9) for a couple of days non-stop in the Week Of Nightmares, I think it's safe to say that Arhats (Minimum Dharma of 10) can do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are some examples of power that an Arhat might have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:20:34-07:00","id":1395552,"title":"","content":"I admittedly have no idea. I'm not the most well-versed when it comes to KotE <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I just remembered the Botthisattvas from Time of Thin Blood/Week of Nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:28:07-07:00","id":1395553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395550#post1395550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are some examples of power that an Arhat might have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Few, but canon sitll has some details:<br /> Description about arhat and founder of Thrashing Dragon, Thousand Crane Mother:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mighty being, she fears little. She lives a life of natural harmony, surrounded by a hush of peace. </div> </div> </div>And 1000 Hells say only an Arhat can singly face a weakened Yama King on Earth <br /> <br /> But materials contradict each other:<br /> 1. Thousand Crane Mother hates madarin to approach her and only allows jina to do this because madarin is &quot;more on her equal&quot;? May mean gap between madarin and archat are not so big as elder and meth?<br /> 2. three 2000+ years old boddhis can hinder an Antes a couple of days, but the exp system shows this age can't purchase ver high level powers because of the expensive traits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T02:29:27-07:00","id":1395554,"title":"","content":"In fact few canon concerns the wan gui of this level, even the boddhi has little<br /> Mind you, Boddhi are equal to 4th gens kindred, and arhat is 3rd gens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T08:47:45-07:00","id":1395604,"title":"","content":"I do not think that Arhats have power equal to 3 generations. I would say that they embody their Dharma in themselves.<br /> We know that in the past they had some power, but because of their pride (or something else) they lost this power. They were the heroes who were supposed to protect the world from Yama King.<br /> Therefore, I think the spiritual component is much more important than the raw power and the scale of their abilities / disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 06-10-2020, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T09:32:37-07:00","id":1395609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395604#post1395604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that Arhats have power equal to 3 generations. I would say that they embody their Dharma in themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some thoughts:<br /> 1. No wan gui are as old as 3rd gens, in fact they are younger than kindred, as a splat, if you don't count history of wan xian.<br /> <br /> 2. I find a strange thing:<br /> The <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Botthisattvas</span></span> still active in modern era are all 2000+ years old, and Blood &amp; Silk says the eldest wan guis active in Middle Age comes from Zhou Dynasty, which are also 2000+ years old. So I think that's one of the reasons why no really old wan gui left on earth: They will ascend or descend when at a certain age, just like mage<br /> <br /> 3. Botthisattvas and Arhats are not equal to Meths and Antes, exactly. They are inhumanly enlightened rather than terrible, they're not mindless monsters like Old Bad Vampires. So yes, it is inappropriate to compare them<br /> <br /> 4. Wan gui are still guardians who protect Middle Kingdom from the Yama Kings, but in a more twisted and special ways, well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:11:32-07:00","id":1395658,"title":"","content":"\u200bAnt are not mindless monsters. They just do not care about many others. I mean, they all have their own goals. But the mindless monster is Wight-Methuselah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395609#post1395609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. I find a strange thing:</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably know where the ancient vampires disappeared. They were all in the power of the Yama Kings. They did something bad after all. They were defeated in the past. They lost their strength and were exiled to Yama, or simply could not fight back from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395609#post1395609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No wan gui are as old as 3rd gens</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that the powers available to them are somewhat less than the powers of the Cainites of 3 generations. 3rd generation is fundamentally different in this from others.<br /> <br /> Their strength comes from Chi control, philosophical thoughts, 2 souls (or 1 soul?) and their own state of being. Wan xian always lived in some kind of &quot;harmony&quot; with the world. They study, ascend to heaven, try to find their lost place in the world. They are warriors, heroes or sages who have gone through many trials and have been gifted with great power. But this force was not supposed to threaten the world. They are warriors, not lords of heaven. Their powers can come more from philosophy than from the raw power of destruction or subjugation of the planet. <br /> <br /> I very much doubt that the kings were so strong that they could not be defeated by an army of 10,000 methuselah / antediluvian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T14:10:51-07:00","id":1395673,"title":"","content":"Only a Mage with Arch-Spheres could hope to defeat an Arhat or use OP wonders like the &quot;Spirit-Nukes&quot; (lol) that the Technocracy used to &quot;defeat&quot; Ravnos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T17:58:05-07:00","id":1395708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395658#post1395658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI very much doubt that the kings were so strong that they could not be defeated by an army of 10,000 methuselah / antediluvian.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the most powerful yama kings, Tou Mu, a spirit from the second age, was killed by Voormas in Judgement of Ascension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T18:03:39-07:00","id":1395709,"title":"","content":"Voormas had appeared in 1000 Hells<br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Page 34, the silent stronghold of Tou Mu<br /> </span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><i>Her honored guest, the chi\u2019n at Voormas, perhaps the greatest of Kali\u2019s children, resides here while he avoids the justice of those he betrayed. </i></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect they had designed ToJ from this time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T02:37:49-07:00","id":1395795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395708#post1395708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the most powerful yama kings, Tou Mu, a spirit from the second age, was killed by Voormas in Judgement of Ascension</div> </div> </div> </div>But he isnt wan xian. <br /> <br /> No one said that all kings are fighters. I doubt that he came and waved his staff and the king died. He should have had reasons to do this, as well as have allies. Otherwise, it would be too ... unreasonable and risky. <br /> As far as I remember, he stole VERY powerful artifacts. He is also not a simple archmage. He is an oracle, an archmage with Arete 7-9, a madman who is afraid of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T14:01:20-07:00","id":1396071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395795#post1395795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he isnt wan xian.<br /> <br /> No one said that all kings are fighters. I doubt that he came and waved his staff and the king died. He should have had reasons to do this, as well as have allies. Otherwise, it would be too ... unreasonable and risky.<br /> As far as I remember, he stole VERY powerful artifacts. He is also not a simple archmage. He is an oracle, an archmage with Arete 7-9, a madman who is afraid of death.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, steal artifacts? Didn't ol' Voorn actually absorb the very essence of the Yama King to stop death itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T20:13:57-07:00","id":1396101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1396071#post1396071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, steal artifacts? Didn't ol' Voorn actually absorb the very essence of the Yama King to stop death itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, he absorbed the very essence of the Yama King<i> to steal the artifact </i>that he then wanted to use in order to stop death. The artifact was in possesion of a spirit/thing that was leagues above Tou Mu in terms of power (that the archmage identified as the real Shiva), and refused to lend it to someone that wasn't a god - Voorn killed the Yama King to &quot;wear&quot; her as a way to convince Shiva that he was divine.<br /> <br /> The moral of the story being: Vormass it's terrible guest","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-12-2020, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-12T21:51:39-07:00","id":1396114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1396101#post1396101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Actually, he absorbed the very essence of the Yama King<i> to steal the artifact </i>that he then wanted to use in order to stop death. The artifact was in possesion of a spirit/thing that was leagues above Tou Mu in terms of power (that the archmage identified as the real Shiva), and refused to lend it to someone that wasn't a god - Voorn killed the Yama King to &quot;wear&quot; her as a way to convince Shiva that he was divine.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25408_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25408\" data-vbnamecard=\"25408\">Alphari</a><br /> <br /> Tou Mu is one of the greatest Yama Kings, a spirits created by Scarlett Queen and Ebon Dragon, one of the most likely candidates of Demon Emperor, who will end the world<br /> <br /> The 1000 Hells says, the GRAND Wan Xian, Lei-Tsung, united with a troop of Wan Xian and JUST destroyed an AVATAR of her<br /> And Lei himself was killed, most of the troop were captured and tortured in the Hell of Tou Mou untill now<br /> <br /> And she was killed by an archmage. who. has. stats<br /> <br /> Well, just show how badass mage is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1396101#post1396101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The moral of the story being: Vormass it's terrible guest </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I was totally shocked when I saw Voormas in The 1000 Hells book, it is a big crossover, a noted npc in another line appeared in the KotE which is not very related <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Another mage in that book, Jizo the Wanderer, is also a terrible guest in Kakuri Hell, he is the only guy who can frighten Emma-O away</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 06-13-2020, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T00:17:38-07:00","id":1396132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alphari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1395795#post1395795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he isnt wan xian. <br /> <br /> No one said that all kings are fighters. I doubt that he came and waved his staff and the king died. He should have had reasons to do this, as well as have allies. Otherwise, it would be too ... unreasonable and risky. <br /> As far as I remember, he stole VERY powerful artifacts. He is also not a simple archmage. He is an oracle, an archmage with Arete 7-9, a madman who is afraid of death.</div> </div> </div> </div> Voormas is (used to be?) an incredibly powerful archmage, yes, but Oracles are beyond even that and act according to fate (or are aspects of?) fate itself. <br /> <br /> Voormas is definitely NOT an Oracle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T12:47:31-07:00","id":1396201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1396132#post1396132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voormas is (used to be?) an incredibly powerful archmage, yes, but Oracles are beyond even that and act according to fate (or are aspects of?) fate itself.<br /> <br /> Voormas is definitely NOT an Oracle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought Oracles we're just a faction of Arch-Mages, why are you casting them as if their different from any other one? They are just Arch-Mages who try to dig in newly Ascended Awakened who have acquired the insights to gain Arch-Spheres- atleast from what I remember from Masters of the Art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T14:25:11-07:00","id":1396212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1396201#post1396201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought Oracles we're just a faction of Arch-Mages, why are you casting them as if their different from any other one? They are just Arch-Mages who try to dig in newly Ascended Awakened who have acquired the insights to gain Arch-Spheres- atleast from what I remember from Masters of the Art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on source. The term Oracle in Mage pre-dates any Archspheres. The most common interpretation of the Oracles is that they are Mages that were about to Ascend, unlocking the mystery of it - but then stopped and instead decided to &quot;stay&quot; and guide others towards Ascension. Note: Mages, not necessarily Arch-mages! - Ascension and Arch-Mageism are never directly linked. On the contrary, it is hinted at that *too* obsessive-compulsive chasing of Arch-knowledge can have actually detremental effects. see: Exemplars, who can never ascend anymore.<br /> <br /> What their unlocking of Ascension actually means in terms of pure power is an absolute undefined unknown, as much as anything about Ascension itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-13-2020, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T20:19:34-07:00","id":1396293,"title":"","content":"Ah thanks for that clear up, I was little confused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T00:59:44-07:00","id":1396327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1395545-can-arhats-combat-mages?p=1396212#post1396212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on source. The term Oracle in Mage pre-dates any Archspheres. The most common interpretation of the Oracles is that they are Mages that were about to Ascend, unlocking the mystery of it - but then stopped and instead decided to &quot;stay&quot; and guide others towards Ascension. Note: Mages, not necessarily Arch-mages! - Ascension and Arch-Mageism are never directly linked. On the contrary, it is hinted at that *too* obsessive-compulsive chasing of Arch-knowledge can have actually detremental effects. see: Exemplars, who can never ascend anymore.<br /> <br /> What their unlocking of Ascension actually means in terms of pure power is an absolute undefined unknown, as much as anything about Ascension itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cOracle&quot; in 1st edtion core is archmage in later editions, indeed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T22:03:25-07:00","id":1396611,"title":"","content":"How are Arhats? Do they mostly just meditate and try to stay out of other people's businesses?<br /> <br /> They also seem pretty decent folks since they are willing to share their wisdom to people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1945,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","user":"Magicballz","date":". 06-15-2020, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-18T20:42:48-07:00","id":1397438,"title":"","content":"Can a high level Wan Kuei combat a mage? Sure, just like any supernatural can fight another. The issue is the relative power levels and the nature of the confrontation. And when it comes to mages in particular I think 'nature' matters alot because of how open ended their powers can be - nothing requires them or forces them to fight a Wan Kuei (or any other ancient vampire) on the Vampire's terms. Archmages would have it easier (although what *KIND* of archmages we're talking about is another issue since its been handled a few different ways I recall) but even one with enough 4-5 dot spheres could be an issue if the Ancient Vampire isn't careful. Luckily many of the really old and powerful ones ARE careful.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}